The sources describe the Nvidia Blackwell GPU architecture as featuring a massive die size of 750mm² with 92.2 billion transistors, 192 Streaming Multiprocessors, and a memory subsystem with L2 bandwidth of approximately 8.7 TB/s. The Blackwell Ultra variant includes two reticle-sized dies connected with a 10 TB/s NV-HBI interface, manufactured on TSMC 4NP with 208B transistors, and HBM3E memory capacity reaching 288 GB with 8 TB/s bandwidth. The embedded Blackwell GPUs feature up to 24GB of GDDR7 VRAM, fifth-generation Tensor Cores with FP4 precision support, and PCIe Gen 5 for double the data ingest speed. The architecture also includes a custom-built four-nanometer manufacturing process and a fifth-generation NVLink network switch providing up to 1.8 terabits per second of bidirectional throughput per GPU.
